deep.reconstruction:
Grothendieck opens a systematic treatment of stratified spaces through 'conical neighbourhoods'. In the title, 'tubulaires' is crossed out in favour of 'côniques'. This is the 'déploiement' programme sketched in Esquisse d'un programme §5. The page sets up the basic object, an abstract ('absolu') conical neighbourhood of a space Y.

Definition. The data are:
- a topological space T containing Y (the 'tube');
- a closed subset Ṫ ⊂ T (the 'bord du tube');
- a continuous action of the topological monoid I=[0,1], under multiplication, on T, written (λ,t)↦λt.

The axioms are:
(a) λy=y for all y∈Y;
(b) 0·T⊂Y. Together with (a), this makes λ↦λ_T an I-parametrised deformation retraction of T onto Y, rel Y.
(c) The square I×Ṫ → T, {0}×Ṫ → Y (with (0,x)↦0·x) is cocartesian in Top. A footnote says this means the induced map from (I×Ṫ) ⊔ Y is surjective and T carries the quotient topology.

Consequence. T ≅ C(f) with f:Ṫ→Y, f(x)=0·x. In the image, Grothendieck writes 'cône de l'application'. The pushout I×Ṫ ∪_{0×Ṫ} Y is in fact the mapping cylinder of f. Under this identification:
- Y ↪ T ↩ Ṫ correspond to but(f) ↪ C(f) ↩ source(f), with Ṫ sitting at level 1;
- the I-action is the one induced on the quotient by λ·(μ,x)=(λμ,x) on I×Ṫ and the trivial action on Y.
So the structure (Y↪T↩Ṫ, I×T→T) is the same thing as a map f:Ṫ→Y together with its cylinder.

Margin note. Axiom (b) becomes superfluous: (c) already contains 0·Ṫ⊂Y, and then 0·T⊂Y follows.

Recovering the boundary. Finally Ṫ is recovered from the action: the interior is T° = T∖Ṫ = ⋃_{λ∈[0,1[} λT. In cylinder coordinates, λT = Y ∪ [0,λ]×Ṫ, so the union is everything except level 1.

What this serves. The next page goes on to:
- the filtrations T_λ = λT;
- the 'épaississements' Ep_ε of the boundary, ≅ [1−ε,1]×Ṫ;
- relative conical neighbourhoods of a closed Y⊂X, where λṪ is the frontier of λT in X.
The evident aim is to describe a stratified space by gluing mapping-cylinder neighbourhoods of strata, as in Esquisse §5.
